"1. Fixed the version-numbering blocker by keeping unaccepted work out of the version list. Juno's R1 suggestions, R2's stopped drafts and tries now live in a small `ArtifactProposal` table from M0, never synced or shared, so every `currentVersion + 1` write path (including Mac 1.6.0's) and time-resolved shares stay correct. R1's exit adds the N0 POST, transaction and `/share` tests.\n2. Fixed the preview XSS blocker. Every preview response must carry a CSP `sandbox` header, refuse non-iframe `Sec-Fetch-Dest` and send `nosniff`, and R2's exit adds a CI test that opens a preview URL top-level. Subdomains are now keyed HMACs, legacy scripted shares are screened (new backfill B11) before public previews turn on, and `taint`/`messageId` move to M0 so \"Run page\" works from R2. \u00a79.5 and \u00a713.6 say to tell the X-01 session now; I couldn't message it, so the owner or releaser has to pass that on.\n3. Fixed the Day-one editing example (the design blocker): \u00a78.3 now states the rule once (edits made while Juno works win field by field; what the request names overrides earlier edits). \u00a71.5 step 5 uses v4 \"Your edits\" then v5 from Juno, the stepper reads \"v4 \u00b7 edited\", and there is a golden test for each case.\n4. Anchored artifacts: the anchor conversation is never synced to any client, a minimal read-only `/a/{id}` ships in R1, and `userId`/`projectId` plus a file-reference index move to M0. All three delete routes and account deletion go through one detaching helper, and the ledger now records the owner even in cascades.\n5. Installed clients: now five protections. The N0 projection also covers REST, saved messages keep the legacy tag form, and field-preserving saves use a per-build key set. N0 devices are counted by auth-token device, and the N0 projection is now permanent. Each capability has a written contract.\n6. Mac and iPhone: N1 cherry-picks glass's row resolver (pinned to `2b1049c5`), which closes X-11/X-12 for Mac and iPhone users who update. Unknown kinds are added without changing the enum. Each file that will conflict in the glass merge has one owner, and the list of requests to the glass session is complete. The iPhone keeps text and colour edits from N1.\n7. Schedule: new R0 on Monday 2026-09-28 (the `7243613f` fix, X-08, X-02, type immutability). R1 and R2 are re-dated for one lane (10-08, 10-22). The owner sees the merged home at R10 (First light, 12-10). No Design pointer row ships. Code's Artifacts row moves to a new R16, motion model v2 moves to Phase 7, and Brand ships in R15.\n8. Surface: header collapse ladder with the arithmetic; the selection controls live in the bottom tool row; the full-window layout is recorded as an explicit amendment to PREMIUM rule 2, with the app sidebar hidden. Other changes: Esc ladder, undo ownership, one Juno write per artifact at a time, History as the activity view, the canvas legend kept out of the accent colour, View Transitions snapshot morph, and a motion table with a token column.\n9. Words and places: eight type nouns (Page becomes App, Markdown is migrated to Doc at Launch), a suggestion vocabulary, a new Appendix C copy table, at most eight places to find a made thing, \"Copy private link\", and one link to hand out. The wireframes are redrawn and labelled by phase, with new WF-8 to WF-11. \u00a714.2 is now eight yes/no product decisions plus a table of engineering defaults.\n10. Every issue (29 engineering, 28 design) is marked fixed in the new Review log at the end of `/Users/liammagnier/Developer/project/juno/docs/design/artifacts-design/04-MERGE-PLAN.md`. Where I took a different route from the suggestion, the log says why: no separate \"Saved\" label, `/a/{id}` sends visitors to the published page instead of the reverse, per-artifact app data named as a gap until Phase 7, and public chat shares made static permanently."